13541| ### `sgitexindex` -- CRIME_RE_TEX indexes with `>> 3` where its three siblings use `>> 1`
13542| 
13543| Found by the codex seat under the **standing license**, while answering a scope question
13544| about a different defect in the same file.
13545| 
13546| **The evidence is the sibling comparison, and it is as strong as this kind of finding gets:**
13547| three arms of one handler do it one way and the fourth does it another.
13548| 
13549| ```c
13550| CRIME_RE_TLB_A / _TLB_B / _TLB_C:  int tlbi = ((relative_addr & 0x1ff) >> 1) & 0xff;
13551| CRIME_RE_TEX:                      int tlbi = ((relative_addr & 0xff)  >> 3) & 0xff;
13552| ```
13553| 
13554| Both index arrays of the same kind �?" `re_tex` is `uint16_t[112]`, and the window
13555| (`>= CRIME_RE_TEX && < CRIME_RE_TEX + 0xe0`) is 224 bytes, which is exactly 112 halfwords. So
13556| window and array correspond one-to-one, and `>> 1` is the byte�+'halfword conversion.
13557| 
13558| **The write loop steps `tlbi++` per halfword, so an 8-byte `sd` writes four entries �?" but
13559| `>> 3` advances the start index by only one per 8-byte step:**
13560| 
13561|     offset 0x00 -> tlbi 0, writes 0,1,2,3
13562|     offset 0x08 -> tlbi 1, writes 1,2,3,4   <- OVERLAPS THREE
13563|     offset 0x10 -> tlbi 2, writes 2,3,4,5   <- OVERLAPS THREE
13564| 
13565| So a guest writing the array sequentially **overwrites three quarters of what it just
13566| wrote**, and the top of the window (`0xdf >> 3` = 27, reaching index 30) leaves **entries
13567| 31..111 unreachable by any access**.
13568| 
13569| `>> 1` is right at both ends �?" `0x00 >> 1` = 0 and `0xdf >> 1` = 111, exactly the last valid
13570| index �?" which is what makes this a typo rather than a design.
13571| 
13572| > **This is NOT the width-kill class and must not be folded into it.** `widthkillclass` is a
13573| > guest *ending the host* by choosing an access size; this is **silent data corruption inside
13574| > a legal, correctly-sized access**. Different class, different fix, different detector �?" the
13575| > round-scope rule's same-class arm fails, so it files rather than joining `#497`.
13576| 
13577| Ranked **med**: silent (nothing announces it, and the guest gets wrong texture data rather
13578| than a dead emulator), but it corrupts only emulated device state, where a host kill ends the
13579| process.
13580| 
13581| **A round owes a rung-3 witness first** �?" the machine and window are already established by
13582| `widthkillclass`'s witness (`-E sgi -e ip32`, TEX at guest `0xb5001600`) �?" **and an
13583| adjacent-offset oracle, because a naive "the `sd` changed something" accept row stays GREEN
13584| under this defect.** The write does land; it lands in the wrong cells and on top of its
13585| neighbour. The row must write two adjacent 8-byte groups and read back the *first*.
